 can exploit this vulnerability by submitting a specially crafted request to a vulnerable system that causes that system to execute arbitrary code. The request allows a cyber actor to take full control over the system. The actor can then steal information, launch ransomware, or conduct other malicious activity.","evidenceUrl":["https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa22-117a","https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/publications/CSRB-Report-on-Log4-July-11-2022_508.pdf","https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2021/12/11/guidance-for-preventing-detecting-and-hunting-for-cve-2021-44228-log4j-2-exploitation/#attacks","https://www.zdnet.com/article/log4j-flaw-attackers-are-making-thousands-of-attempts-to-exploit-this-severe-vulnerability/"],"wasDerivedFrom":["https://github.com/center-for-threat-informed-defense/mappings-explorer/tree/ddc842aa48c871cbfc2219cdbb842e9a4e155afe"],"technique":{"@id":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1505/003/","@type":"AttackTechnique","techniqueId":"T1505.003","name":"Web Shell","tactic":[{"@id":"https://attack.mitre.org/tactics/TA0003/","@type":"AttackTactic","tacticId":"TA0003","shortname":"persistence"}]}}],"wasDerivedFrom":["https://github.com/cisagov/kev-data/tree/0cca62ed469c333a45760beeaf35fcc53352aedd"]}